Ports upstream PR vllm-project/vllm#64137 (merged 2026-10-29, after the 0.33.0 branch) to this pin.

On 0.33.0, vllm #61451 changed the bonus-logit check in _compute_local_logits_stats_kernel and
_compute_local_residual_mass_kernel to take num_logits, which changes with the batch, where 0.32.0 passed the
constant num_speculative_steps. Both are plain @triton.jit kernels, so Triton specializes the integer and compiles
a new variant when the batch's logit count changes class. The rejection-sampler warm-up compiles one request's
shape, therefore the first concurrent requests compiled the kernel again inside serving: on an RTX 3090 with the
single-user launcher's defaults and a cold cache, the port logged _compute_local_logits_stats_kernel as a JIT
compilation during inference about 7 s into its first 64-way burst, and 0.32.0 did not.

The PR marks num_logits do_not_specialize on both kernels, so one compiled kernel serves every batch.

Applied unchanged: the PR's single hunk set cherry-picks onto 0.33.0 without conflicts.

Kind: fix
What: the rejection sampler's logits-stats and residual-mass kernels no longer recompile per batch size
  (num_logits not specialized)
Upstream: vllm #64137 (merged); the regression is from vllm #61451
Cut-against: 0.33.0
Retires-when: the pin that carries #64137

